 "_comment": [
  "Frozen ledger states for scripts/selftest_instagram.py and for the human-review",
  "previews. FROZEN ON PURPOSE: a card quotes running aggregates, so testing against",
  "the live ledgers would break the first time any pick grades — a false alarm, not a",
  "regression. Same reasoning as qualified_social_golden.json.",
  "",
  "Shapes mirror production exactly (verified against scripts/selftest_social.py's",
  "QUAL/DAILY and against grade.py): the Qualified ledger carries pnl / units /",
  "units_net / roi_pct; the Daily ledger carries pnl_paper / pnl_staked /",
  "units_staked / paper_basis and paper_units_net / paper_roi_pct, and has NO pnl,",
  "units, units_net or roi_pct at all. On a VOID, grade.py only assigns final_score",
  "in the non-void branch, so the key is ABSENT rather than null — mirrored here.",
  "",
  "Every 'daily_*' scenario ships an EMPTY qualified ledger, because select_recap()",
  "prefers Qualified whenever it has a settled entry for the date; an empty one is",
  "what forces the Daily Pick path."
 ],
